    {
      "id": "sCxMafRD6DZvjBv9hW7wI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 522.1428833007812,
      "y": 3605.2857360839844,
      "width": 1047.1427001953125,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 540466211,
      "version": 143,
      "versionNonce": 223514797,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779051053118,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What each component does\nControl Plane components:\n\na)API Server — The single front door for everything. Every kubectl command, every internal\ncomponent, every external client talks to the API server first. It validates requests and\nstores results in etcd.\n\nb)etcd — A distributed key-value store. The single source of truth for the entire cluster.\nStores all resource definitions, current state, and desired state.\n\nc)Scheduler — Watches for newly created pods that have no assigned node, and assigns them to\nthe best available node based on resources, constraints, and policies.\n\nd)Controller Manager — Runs a set of controllers (ReplicaSet controller, Node controller, Job\ncontroller, etc.) that continuously watch actual state vs desired state and reconcile any\ndifferences.\n\nWorker Node components:\n\na)Kubelet — An agent running on every node. It receives pod specs from the API server and\nensures the described containers are running and healthy.\n\nb)Kube-proxy — Maintains network rules on each node. Handles routing so that a Service (a\nstable virtual IP) forwards traffic to the right pod(s).\n\nc)Container Runtime — The actual engine that runs containers (containerd, CRI-O, or Docker).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What each component does\nControl Plane components:\n\na)API Server — The single front door for everything. Every kubectl command, every internal component, every external client talks to the API server first. It validates requests and stores results in etcd.\n\nb)etcd — A distributed key-value store. The single source of truth for the entire cluster. Stores all resource definitions, current state, and desired state.\n\nc)Scheduler — Watches for newly created pods that have no assigned node, and assigns them to the best available node based on resources, constraints, and policies.\n\nd)Controller Manager — Runs a set of controllers (ReplicaSet controller, Node controller, Job controller, etc.) that continuously watch actual state vs desired state and reconcile any differences.\n\nWorker Node components:\n\na)Kubelet — An agent running on every node. It receives pod specs from the API server and ensures the described containers are running and healthy.\n\nb)Kube-proxy — Maintains network rules on each node. Handles routing so that a Service (a stable virtual IP) forwards traffic to the right pod(s).\n\nc)Container Runtime — The actual engine that runs containers (containerd, CRI-O, or Docker).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
