    {
      "id": "g1NGfFj8rwzOBo3qghupK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1024.195479814044,
      "y": 10126.741408986803,
      "width": 561,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1452395341,
      "version": 231,
      "versionNonce": 112161261,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779055007066,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "But the thing is \npods in k8 are ephemeral \nwhich means the crash and restart\nand when a new pod / pod restarts it gets assign \na new ip address-which becomes inconvenient to keep\ntrack of everytime the pod changes ip",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "But the thing is \npods in k8 are ephemeral \nwhich means the crash and restart\nand when a new pod / pod restarts it gets assign \na new ip address-which becomes inconvenient to keep\ntrack of everytime the pod changes ip",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "C7EAFhr_kaO8awl-Etx2h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 482.6599031493778,
      "y": 10443.349976243733,
      "width": 1144,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ag",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1015401251,
      "version": 505,
      "versionNonce": 813036707,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "BtdsDRBpR_c-6tv8pxunx",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1779055129955,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is very similar to docker container when we spin up a docker container they both become part of \na docker0 network isolated to each other the container cannot talk with each other via dns we have \nto use ip addresss of the container and then when container restarts it creates a new ip so we solve\nthis via docker-compose which automatically puts them in the same network so that they can talk to each \nother via there container name (Dns)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is very similar to docker container when we spin up a docker container they both become part of \na docker0 network isolated to each other the container cannot talk with each other via dns we have \nto use ip addresss of the container and then when container restarts it creates a new ip so we solve\nthis via docker-compose which automatically puts them in the same network so that they can talk to each \nother via there container name (Dns)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
